# The KMS-compatible service (services/kms/, .kiro/specs/kms-compatible-api/).
# Sourced from the top-level Kconfig's "Service Modules" menu.

config KMS
	bool "KMS-compatible key management service"
	default n
	depends on HSM && IAM
	help
	  Builds the services/kms/ module: AWS KMS's JSON 1.1 API, so the AWS
	  CLI, the SDKs and the AWS Encryption SDK work against it unchanged,
	  with every key's material a non-extractable object on the virtual
	  HSM and every request authorized by IAM with the key's policy. So
	  far the module holds the pinned botocore model, its generated shape
	  tables, the coverage check and the kms_node placeholder (task 1);
	  the catalog, the HSM binding and the API follow. Needs the HSM and
	  IAM modules. Off by default like every new module
	  (services/README.md). See .kiro/specs/kms-compatible-api/.
